  "sources": [
    {
      "source": "HOKFIRE",
      "url": "https://www.hokfire.com/",
      "field": "abilities",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "Passive",
          "name": "The Great Sage",
          "desc": "Using skills enhances the next Basic Attack to a dash strike that deals extra damage. Base Critical Rate increases, but Critical Damage decreases."
        },
        {
          "type": "Skill 1",
          "name": "Protective Shroud",
          "desc": "Gains increased Movement Speed and blocks the damage and effects of the next enemy hero skill. After a successful block, gains temporary invulnerability to damage andskills, as well as a shield."
        },
        {
          "type": "Skill 2",
          "name": "Furious Advance",
          "desc": "Wukong shifts in the target direction. Hitting units during the shift will trigger another shift and grant a Movement Speed boost. The shift deals damage to monsters, and grievous damage to monsters at low Health."
        },
        {
          "type": "Ultimate",
          "name": "Golden Cudgel",
          "desc": "Launches enemies in range, damaging and placing 3 marks on them. BasicAttack removes 1 mark and deals extra damage every time."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "source": "HOKFIRE",
      "url": "https://www.hokfire.com/",
      "field": "guide",
      "content": {
        "pros": [
          "High burst damage",
          "Great mobility",
          "Strong snowball potential"
        ],
        "cons": [
          "Very Squishy",
          "Weak against tanks",
          "Vulnerable to crowd control"
        ],
        "gameplay_tips": "## Early Game\nWukong has decent early jungle clear speed with his Skill 2 mobility and empowered auto attacks. He also has a lot of burst damage early on, and great crowd control with his Ultimate Golden Cudgel, so you can look for early ganks to try and snowball the early game; however, if you make a mistake and fall behind, it becomes extremely difficult to come back into the game.\n\n## Teamfights\nIn teamfights, as an assassin, Wukong wants to hide in bushes and engage from unexpected angles. You don't want to be the first one to engage in the front line. You need to completely ignore the tanks and focus on their Marksman or Mage to one-shot them with your burst combo. This is your main goal; failing to do so will lose you the teamfight and potentially the game.\n\n## Tips & Tricks\nAlways basic attack after using a Skill to deal bonus damage with Wukong's passive\nSave Skill 1 for blocking important enemy skills\nYou can use Skill 2 to bounce off minions or teammates to help escape or catch up to enemies"
      }
    },
    {
      "source": "Kurohiko",
      "url": "https://hok.kurohiko.id/",
      "field": "tactical_tips",
      "content": "Jangan cast skill ke Wukong pas skill 1 aktif. Hero tipis selalu perhatiin posisinya dan jaga jarak."
    },
    {
      "source": "HoKStats",
      "url": "https://hokstats.gg/heroes/wukong/",
      "field": "guide",
      "content": {
        "skills": [
          {
            "name": "The Great Sage",
            "description": "Using skills enhances the next Basic Attack to a dash strike that deals extra damage. He has a higher base Critical Rate but lower base Critical Damage than other heroes.",
            "type": "passive"
          },
          {
            "name": "Protective Shroud",
            "description": "Gains Movement Speed and blocks the next enemy skill's damage and effects. Upon a successful block, grants temporary damage and skill invulnerability along with a shield.",
            "type": "skill1"
          },
          {
            "name": "Furious Advance",
            "description": "Dashes in the target direction. If he dashes into an enemy, he'll dash again and gain Movement Speed. The dash deals damage to monsters, and grievous damage to monsters at low Health.",
            "type": "skill2"
          },
          {
            "name": "Golden Cudgel",
            "description": "Launches enemies within range, damaging and placing 3 marks on them. Enemies lose 1 mark and take extra damage when hit by his Basic Attack.",
            "type": "ultimate"
          }
        ],
        "pick_when": [
          "The map shape favors gank routes, where mobility translates directly into kills",
          "The enemy team has multiple high-mobility threats that need to be locked down before they reach your backline",
          "The enemy draft includes Dun, Lian Po, and Xiang Yu, who appear in counter data as matchups Wukong can pressure."
        ],
        "avoid_when": [
          "Enemy peel is strong and Wukong cannot reach the backline without dying first",
          "Your team lacks the follow-up damage to convert your control windows into kills",
          "The enemy already drafted Agudo, Gao, and Heino, who counter data identifies as direct answers to Wukong."
        ],
        "power_spikes": [
          "Early game: jungle clear into level-4 ganks is the first window where Wukong can translate routes into kills.",
          "Mid game: with cooldown reduction online, gap-close skills come back fast enough to chain into multiple fights",
          "Late game: full build online, Wukong reaches the spike public guides describe — extended fights favor him once items are completed."
        ],
        "common_mistakes": [
          "Diving while enemy hard control is still up, which directly counters Wukong's engage.",
          "Throwing Furious Advance on the front-line tank instead of saving it for backline carries.",
          "Ignoring Agudo and Gao on the enemy team when picking fights — counter data flags them as direct answers, so engage timing must respect their cooldowns.",
          "Pathing predictably and getting tracked by the enemy jungler — vary first clear and rotate based on ward placement rather than muscle memory."
        ],
